"Wireless charging has no cable and no input-current sensor, so there is nothing to measure." = "无线充电既没有线缆也没有输入电流传感器，没有可测的对象。";
"Waiting for the phone to draw enough to measure a drop. Below about 150 mA there is nothing to divide." = "等待手机取用到足够电流才能测出压降。低于约 150 mA 时没有可除的数。";
"The rail is collapsing under load. The phone is taking well under what the charger offered, and the voltage at the port is far below what was negotiated — the current is being held down to stop it falling further. Try another cable on this charger: if the drop shrinks, it was the cable." = "供电轨在负载下正在塌陷。手机取用的电流远低于充电器给出的能力，而端口电压远低于协商值 —— 电流被压住，以免电压继续下跌。换一根线缆试试：如果压降变小，问题就在原来那根线。";
"Fitted over %@ of current swing, with %@ of it on the line." = "在 %@ 的电流变化区间上拟合得出，其中 %@ 落在有效范围内。";
"From one sample, against the negotiated %@. That figure is a ceiling rather than a measurement, so read this as an order of magnitude. Once the current moves — the taper past 80%, thermal throttling, the phone's own load — it is replaced by a fit that needs no reference at all." = "来自单次采样，参照的是协商值 %@。那个协商值是上限而非实测，所以只能当作数量级来看。一旦电流发生变化（80% 之后的涓流、温控降频、手机自身负载），就会换成无需任何参照的拟合结果。";
"Either way this is the whole path — the charger's own regulation, the cable and both plugs — not the cable alone, so it reads best as a comparison between cables on the same charger." = "无论哪种算法，这里量到的都是整条通路 —— 充电器自身的稳压、线缆、以及两端插头 —— 而不只是线缆。所以它最适合用来在同一只充电器上横向比较不同的线。";
"Low. Nothing in this connection is holding the charge back." = "偏低。这条连接上没有任何环节在拖慢充电。";
"Ordinary for a long or thin cable. It costs a little power as heat, and at these currents it is unlikely to change how fast the phone charges." = "对偏长或偏细的线缆来说是正常水平。会以发热的形式损失一点功率，但在当前电流下不太会影响充电速度。";
"High for a charging path. A thinner or longer cable, a worn plug or a loose fit all look like this. Trying another cable on the same charger is the way to tell which." = "对充电路径来说偏高。线太细或太长、插头磨损、接触松动都会是这样。换一根线插在同一只充电器上，就能分辨到底是哪种。";
